    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been trying this box breathing thing (inhale 4, hold 4, exhale 4, hold 4) lately to help with stress. can u explain what's actually happening in the body when i do that? like how does it affect the nervous system or stuff like cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing, also known as square breathing, helps regulate the autonomic nervous system (ANS) by balancing between the sympathetic (stress response) and parasympathetic (rest and digest) nervous systems. When you inhale, exhale, and hold your breath, you activate a calming effect on the brain, specifically releasing neurotransmitters like dopamine and serotonin while reducing cortisol levels in the body. This leads to reduced stress, improved focus, and a more balanced nervous system overall.",
      "source": "target",
